# Round mtppf: the MTP arm's prompt call walks the draft's warmup through the store's append alone
# (MtpMode::Store) instead of whole eager walks. Same binary, two arms by the draft lever, as the
# q38mtp-tg sitting (docs/cards/q38mtp-tg.card; its log: plain pp512 619.2 / pp4096 612.9,
# mtp 473.6 / 458.3, 3 rounds, prose, A6000 plan a, C 4352).
# Decomposing that sitting's gap, per round from its `stat prompt host` and `time prompt` rows:
# - the union term: the draft's card reserve (place.rs plan_mtp_with, the draft's 2.82 GB) moves
#   target slots to the host, host_slots 115,726 -> 123,608 (P 512) and 908,274 -> 981,105 (P 4096)
#   in every round; union_ms +27..+35 (mean +29.8) and +330..+435 (mean +375.8) ms. This round does
#   not touch it.
# - the warmup: the rest, +224 ms (P 512) and +1,881 ms (P 4096) over 65 and 513 eager walks of up
#   to 8 rows, 3.45 and 3.67 ms a walk (the ubatch is the whole prompt, so the walks run after the
#   target's one unit, serial on the card, with nothing under them). A warm row's only lasting
#   effect is its keys and values; the store walk keeps embed, pack, eh_proj (4 launches of the
#   13.9 MB matrix), the attention site's mix, q, k, v and the append: 13 launches and ~95 MB a
#   walk, against the whole walk's ~39 launches and ~1.2 GB (the full head's 675 MB, ~80 routed
#   slots of 5.2 MB, the dense rest). At the whole walk's measured 2x over its byte floor the store
#   walk is 0.15-0.35 ms [derived]; band 0.10-0.50 ms, 51-257 ms at P 4096 and 7-33 ms at P 512.
# New MTP arm [derived]: P 4096 6,682 + 330..435 + 51..257 = 7,063..7,374 ms against 6,682:
# -9.4..-5.4 %; P 512 827 + 27..35 + 7..33 = 861..895 ms against 827: -7.5..-3.9 % (printed, not
# decided: the last sitting's plain pp512 rows scatter ~1.9 %, h ~4 % at 3 rounds). The band below is
# P 4096's, the headline row with the smaller scatter.
# The runner (wall: the q38mtp-tg sitting took 6 min for the same 12 processes, 22:21:50-22:27:44):
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/mtppf-pp.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512 prose:512@BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp prose:4096 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp
kind: ab
question: does walking the draft's warmup through the store's append alone close the MTP arm's
  prompt gap down to the draft's card reserve (the union term), as the store walk's cost predicts?
term: pp tok/s @ P=4096 (prose:4096, the time prompt row), n=96, ctx 4352 (BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352),
  A6000, plan a (card experts), BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp against unset, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -9.5..-5.0
rounds: 3
sd: 0.55 % the q38mtp-tg sitting's pp4096 rows (docs/cards/q38mtp-tg.card), plain/mtp paired ratio
  SD 0.75 % over 3 rounds, divided by the square root of 2
condition: one binary, both arms of a P in one lease, a fresh process per load group, the host set
  and the PLE table warm (majflt near 0), no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row; the mtp arm's load line
  names draft=mtp and head=full; each arm's stat prompt host line gives host_slots 908,274 (plain)
  and 981,105 (mtp) at P 4096, 115,726 and 123,608 at P 512 — the same placement as the q38mtp-tg
  sitting, so the union term is that sitting's; the store the warmup leaves reads as before: the mtp
  arm's decode at prose:512 near that sitting's 81.94 tok/s (a store off by bits drops the
  acceptance toward the plain 51.4) and each arm's distinct_tokens the plain arm's (70 at P 512, 61
  at P 4096)
decide-in: land mtppf; the warmup is closed to the store walk's and the gap left is the draft's card
  reserve; the MTP default is then decode +26..+59 % against this pp, and the next lever is the
  reserve (the draft's 2.67 GB of routed experts on the card), a placement round
decide-below: the store walk costs more than 0.5 ms or a term outside the walk and the union moved:
  read each arm's stat prompt host union_ms first (+330..+435 ms at P 4096); inside that band, nsys
  one MTP prompt call at P 4096 before any change
decide-above: the union term landed less than +330 ms on the wall or the store walk is under 0.1 ms:
  compare both arms' host_slots and union_ms with this card's, then re-derive the union's share of
  the prompt wall from one BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 run before the next round
